{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>If</b> — Israel sinned with Jeroboam, who feared lest the kingship come to the house of David; therefore he made two calves at the two ends of the land of Israel. Why should Judah be guilty, having abandoned the Temple that is in its portion, to go to a distant place for idolatry? And the prophet rebukes them: \"Let not Judah be guilty, and do not come to Gilgal, and do not go up to Beth-Aven\" — it is Beth-El, on account of the calf that Jeroboam placed there. It is written in the Torah: \"and you shall swear by His name,\" and the meaning is \"you shall fear YHWH your Elohim\" — so as not to transtract negative commandments, not out of fear of a king or rumor or bodily harm, but only out of fear of HaShem. \"And Him shall you serve\" — a positive commandment, some with the mouth and some with deed. \"And in Him you shall cling\" — in the thought of the heart, so that not a moment pass, to the extent of his ability, without his heart pondering the deeds of HaShem and His wonders — among the supernal, the lower, and the nether beings, and in the signs of the prophets. And after he clings to HaShem, he is obligated to mention HaShem in all his words and to swear by His name, so that all who hear him, the created beings, understand that he clings to the love of HaShem, and always His name and remembrance are fluent in his mouth out of his love for Him, and all the people hear and learn from him love and fear. And such is the way of the prophets, that they swear, like David and Elijah and Elisha; and similar is every expression of \"go, swear.\" And so the meaning of \"why should you fear\" — since you are sons of HaShem and you go to Beth-Aven, it is better that you do neither this nor that. Or its interpretation is set against \"deception\" mentioned at the beginning of the passage."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:11.812377484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}